      "jobId": "decf35ba-279a-4524-a7aa-54ef7923b920",
      "question": "Which five branches held the most deposits (checking and savings balances) at the end of September 2026, and how much did each hold?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:19:42.410390Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:19:48.117786Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "| Branch ID | Branch Name | City | Region | Total Deposits (USD) |\n|-----------|-------------|------|--------|----------------------|\n| BR01 | Harborview Main Street | Harborview | Harbor Coast | 2,696,292.11 |\n| BR07 | Eastgate | Cedar Falls | Metro | 2,161,310.28 |\n| BR02 | Marina District | Harborview | Harbor Coast | 1,982,872.79 |\n| BR18 | Granite Falls | Granite Falls | Highlands | 1,579,240.79 |\n| BR05 | Union Square | Cedar Falls | Metro | 1,486,017.10 |\n\nThese are the five branches with the highest combined checking and savings balances as of September 30, 2026. The Harborview Main Street branch (BR01) held the most deposits at approximately $2.7 million, followed by Eastgate (BR07) at $2.16 million. [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Structured retrieval result — financial_services_banking — evidence `hermes-receipt:92b389a6cde108a8d4a92cd8bfe609b1acec4dd25d9a8e925e57376dd8e3f59a`",
